{"kind":"message","text":"I've successfully fixed the user role dropdown selector issue in the WordPress plugin. \n\n**Problem Identified:**\nThe dropdown was using [`get_editable_roles()`](src/aiplugin5055/Admin/CampaignsView.php:487) which only returns roles that the current user can edit, not all available WordPress roles.\n\n**Solution Implemented:**\nChanged the code in [`CampaignsView.php`](src/aiplugin5055/Admin/CampaignsView.php:487) to use `wp_roles()->roles` instead, which retrieves all available WordPress user roles.\n\n**What Changed:**\n- Line 487: Replaced `$editable_roles = \\get_editable_roles();` with `$all_roles = \\wp_roles()->roles;`\n- Line 488: Updated the foreach loop to use `$all_roles` instead of `$editable_roles`\n\nThe security filtering remains intact - the code still skips privileged roles (those with `edit_posts` or `manage_options` capabilities) to prevent security issues, as required by PRD Section 32. Now the dropdown will display all available non-privileged user roles in your WordPress installation.","is_error":false,"ts":"2026-08-21T15:55:42.615Z"}
{"kind":"message","text":"I've successfully fixed the user role dropdown selector issue in the WordPress plugin. \n\n**Problem Identified:**\nThe dropdown was using [`get_editable_roles()`](src/aiplugin5055/Admin/CampaignsView.php:487) which only returns roles that the current user can edit, not all available WordPress roles.\n\n**Solution Implemented:**\nChanged the code in [`CampaignsView.php`](src/aiplugin5055/Admin/CampaignsView.php:487) to use `wp_roles()->roles` instead, which retrieves all available WordPress user roles.\n\n**What Changed:**\n- Line 487: Replaced `$editable_roles = \\get_editable_roles();` with `$all_roles = \\wp_roles()->roles;`\n- Line 488: Updated the foreach loop to use `$all_roles` instead of `$editable_roles`\n\nThe security filtering remains intact - the code still skips privileged roles (those with `edit_posts` or `manage_options` capabilities) to prevent security issues, as required by PRD Section 32. Now the dropdown will display all available non-privileged user roles in your WordPress installation.","is_error":false,"ts":"2026-08-21T15:55:42.634Z"}
